{"id": "660ab1ed-1354-4fa3-aeb6-108738fe8b60", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "This is a broad multi-dimensional audit across several independent data sources (Firehose stream configs, CloudWatch metrics for delivery health/performance, and service quotas). Let me split this into parallel research efforts rather than pulling it all into my own context.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_OKo4nQVcq14MPBiEoGswNZ", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Perform a security and reliability configuration audit of all Amazon Data Firehose delivery streams in us-east-1 for account 012345678901_1.",
  "context": "User wants a full operational review of Firehose covering security, reliability, delivery health, performance, cost, and service quotas, with each finding rated by severity (e.g. Critical/High/Medium/Low/Informational). This slice covers the static configuration-based dimensions: security and reliability. Use use_aws with service_name='firehose' (list_delivery_streams, describe_delivery_stream) to enumerate streams and their full configs.",
  "resources": ["Amazon Data Firehose delivery streams, us-east-1, account 012345678901_1"],
  "timeframe": "current state (not time-series)",
  "criteria": "For SECURITY: check server-side encryption (SSE) status/key type (AWS-owned vs customer KMS), IAM role permissions attached to each stream (overly permissive roles), VPC delivery configuration for destinations that support it (e.g. OpenSearch), source/destination TLS, resource-based access, logging configuration (CloudWatch error logging enabled/disabled), and whether any stream uses direct PUT vs KDS source with implications. For RELIABILITY: check destination type and backup/failover config (e.g. S3 backup for failed records, retry duration settings), buffering hints (size/interval), compression settings, data format conversion errors, dynamic partitioning error handling, and delivery stream status (ACTIVE/CREATING/DELETING/failed states). List every stream found with its key configuration attributes. Rate each finding by severity and explain the reasoning briefly."
}"}, "type": "tool_use"}, {"id": "tooluse_tLmLhbvaDiTSv5sZXPgqXu", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Analyze Amazon Data Firehose delivery health and performance metrics in CloudWatch for all delivery streams in us-east-1, account 012345678901_1, over the past 7 days.",
  "context": "User wants a full operational review of Firehose covering security, reliability, delivery health, performance, cost, and service quotas, with each finding rated by severity. This slice covers delivery health and performance using CloudWatch metrics (namespace AWS/Firehose). First enumerate delivery streams via use_aws firehose list_delivery_streams if needed to get stream names, then pull metrics per stream.",
  "resources": ["Amazon Data Firehose delivery streams, us-east-1, account 012345678901_1", "CloudWatch namespace AWS/Firehose"],
  "timeframe": "now-7d to now (2026-09-30T19:18:00Z to 2026-10-07T19:18:00Z)",
  "criteria": "For DELIVERY HEALTH: DeliveryToS3.Success, DeliveryToS3.DataFreshness, DeliveryToSplunk/DeliveryToHttpEndpoint/DeliveryToOpenSearch success rates as applicable to destination type, ThrottledRecords, DataReadFromKinesisStream freshness if KDS source, backup delivery success. For PERFORMANCE: IncomingBytes, IncomingRecords, IncomingPutRequests, throughput vs throttling limits, SucceedProcessing/ExecuteProcessing duration for Lambda transforms, PutRequestsPerSecond, BytesPerSecond relative to limits. Flag any metric showing failures, high data freshness lag (staleness), throttling events, or Lambda processing errors. Rate each finding by severity (Critical/High/Medium/Low) with brief reasoning. Report stream names with every finding."
}"}, "type": "tool_use"}, {"id": "tooluse_ofAc1KuSNY4qSxtVcGB1cQ", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine current Amazon Data Firehose resource usage versus AWS service quotas in us-east-1 for account 012345678901_1, and surface cost-relevant configuration signals.",
  "context": "User wants a full operational review of Firehose covering security, reliability, delivery health, performance, cost, and service quotas, with each finding rated by severity. This slice covers service quotas and cost dimensions.",
  "resources": ["Amazon Data Firehose delivery streams, us-east-1, account 012345678901_1", "Service Quotas service code firehose"],
  "timeframe": "current state",
  "criteria": "For SERVICE QUOTAS: use use_aws service_name='service-quotas' list_service_quotas (and list_aws_default_service_quotas as fallback) for service code 'firehose' to find quota values such as number of delivery streams per region, throughput limits (MB/s and records/sec per stream for direct PUT vs KDS source), and compare against the actual count of delivery streams found (use firehose list_delivery_streams). Flag if stream count is approaching the per-region limit. For COST: note any streams using data format conversion (Lambda invocations cost), dynamic partitioning (incurs additional cost), compression settings (CPU/cost tradeoff), small buffer size/interval settings leading to higher PUT request costs, and any streams with error/backup S3 buckets that could indicate retried/duplicated cost. Rate each finding by severity with brief reasoning."
}"}, "type": "tool_use"}], "created_at": null}
